# Files the pre-commit file size check (scripts/check-file-size.mjs) does not measure: anything an agent does not
# write or edit by hand. One gitignore-style glob per line: `#` starts a comment, a pattern with no `/` matches that name
# at any depth (`*.min.*`), a pattern with a `/` is anchored at the repo root, a trailing `/` means a directory and
# everything under it, `**` crosses directories, a leading `!` puts a path back. The last matching line wins.
# A file whose first 10 lines say `@generated` or `DO NOT EDIT` is skipped too, and so are binary files and symlinks,
# so images, fonts and the PNG screenshots need no line here. Add a path here only when no agent writes it by hand.

# Lockfiles: written by the package manager
package-lock.json
npm-shrinkwrap.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lock
bun.lockb
Cargo.lock
Gemfile.lock
poetry.lock
Pipfile.lock
composer.lock
uv.lock
go.sum

# Build output and tool caches (most are also in .gitignore; listed so a forced add is still skipped)
dist/
build/
coverage/
.vite/
dev-dist/
node_modules/
.wrangler/
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated code, minified bundles and source maps
*.generated.*
*.gen.*
*.min.*
*.map

# SVG is text, not a binary, so the binary skip does not cover it (favicon.svg)
*.svg

# Data that a tool writes or a person pastes in: snapshots, fixtures, and the journey evidence (which the runner writes
# outside the repo unless VDT_EVIDENCE points inside it)
*.snap
__snapshots__/
fixtures/
e2e/evidence/

# The social card record: `node scripts/check-og.mjs --write` produces it, nobody edits it by hand
scripts/og/og-image.inputs.json
